user32: readable text in standard controls under a dark palette (Lightroom About box)

Lightroom Classic's About box drew its labels and its Legal Notices / Credits buttons as black text
on a dark box (GitHub issue Neutron#10). Both go through MFC: the parent answers WM_CTLCOLORSTATIC
with black text and a COLOR_BTNFACE brush, and the buttons are painted into an off-screen memory
DC with black text and a BTNFACE background. On Windows COLOR_BTNFACE is light gray (240), so it
reads; with Neutron's dark palette it is 43. The palette cannot simply be lightened: MFC caches it
at startup and Lightroom's menus are drawn from the same table, so they turned light gray too (the
2026-08 attempt, reverted).

So fix the text, not the palette. DrawTextExW now draws in the palette's matching text color
(COLOR_BTNTEXT / COLOR_WINDOWTEXT) when all of these hold:
  - the DC's background color IS the palette's button face (or window color),
  - the app's text color has under 2:1 contrast against it, and the palette's has more,
  - the DC belongs to a Button or Static window -- or is a memory DC on the button face,
    which is how MFC paints its buttons.
Text that already reads is never touched, and with Windows' default palette dark text on the
light face always reads, so the rule only ever acts where the result was unreadable.

Verified with a test program (six cases: black-on-BTNFACE in a Static and in a memory DC change;
black-on-white, palette-text-on-BTNFACE, a custom window and a white memory DC do not): before,
the two black-on-dark cases fail; after, all six pass. In Lightroom Classic the labels and buttons
are readable and the File/Edit/Develop menus look the same.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

--- a/dlls/user32/text.c
+++ b/dlls/user32/text.c
@@ -862,8 +862,8 @@
  * the allowance in DrawTextExA.
  */
 #define MAX_BUFFER 1024
-INT WINAPI DrawTextExW( HDC hdc, LPWSTR str, INT i_count,
-                        LPRECT rect, UINT flags, LPDRAWTEXTPARAMS dtp )
+static INT draw_text_ex_w( HDC hdc, LPWSTR str, INT i_count,
+                           LPRECT rect, UINT flags, LPDRAWTEXTPARAMS dtp )
 {
     SIZE size;
     const WCHAR *strPtr;
@@ -1072,6 +1072,68 @@
     return ret;
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON (GitHub issue Neutron#10): unreadable text in standard controls under a dark palette.
+ *
+ * Lightroom Classic's About box draws its labels (Static) and buttons through MFC, which sets the
+ * text to black and the background to COLOR_BTNFACE. On Windows that face is light gray (240), so
+ * the text reads; with Neutron's dark palette it is 43, and the text was black on dark gray. MFC
+ * reads the palette once at startup and Lightroom's menus are drawn from the same table, so making
+ * COLOR_BTNFACE light again would turn the menus light too (the 2026-08 global attempt did).
+ *
+ * So fix the text, not the palette: when text is drawn into a Button or Static window (or MFC's
+ * off-screen buffer for one), on a
+ * background that IS the palette's button face or window color, in a color with almost no contrast
+ * against it, draw it in the palette's matching text color instead. Text that already reads is
+ * never touched, and on Windows' default palette dark text on a light face always reads, so this
+ * only ever acts where the result was unreadable. */
+static int neutron_luma1000( COLORREF c )
+{
+    /* sRGB relative luminance x1000, gamma approximated as 2 (good enough for a threshold) */
+    int r = GetRValue(c), g = GetGValue(c), b = GetBValue(c);
+    return (2126 * r * r + 7152 * g * g + 722 * b * b) / (255 * 255 * 10);
+}
+
+static BOOL neutron_contrast_poor( COLORREF a, COLORREF b )
+{
+    int la = neutron_luma1000( a ), lb = neutron_luma1000( b );
+    int hi = max( la, lb ), lo = min( la, lb );
+    return (hi + 50) * 10 < (lo + 50) * 20;   /* contrast ratio below 2:1 */
+}
+
+static COLORREF neutron_readable_control_text( HDC hdc )
+{
+    static const WCHAR buttonW[] = {'B','u','t','t','o','n',0}, staticW[] = {'S','t','a','t','i','c',0};
+    COLORREF text = GetTextColor( hdc ), bk = GetBkColor( hdc ), fix;
+    WCHAR cls[16];
+    HWND hwnd;
+
+    if (text == CLR_INVALID || bk == CLR_INVALID) return CLR_INVALID;
+    if (bk == GetSysColor( COLOR_BTNFACE )) fix = GetSysColor( COLOR_BTNTEXT );
+    else if (bk == GetSysColor( COLOR_WINDOW )) fix = GetSysColor( COLOR_WINDOWTEXT );
+    else return CLR_INVALID;
+    if (!neutron_contrast_poor( text, bk ) || neutron_contrast_poor( fix, bk )) return CLR_INVALID;
+    /* MFC paints its buttons into an off-screen memory DC and copies it in, so that DC has no
+     * window. Accept it only on the button face itself, the exact color MFC sets for a button. */
+    if (!(hwnd = NtUserWindowFromDC( hdc )))
+        return (GetObjectType( hdc ) == OBJ_MEMDC && bk == GetSysColor( COLOR_BTNFACE )) ? fix : CLR_INVALID;
+    if (!GetClassNameW( hwnd, cls, ARRAY_SIZE(cls) )) return CLR_INVALID;
+    if (wcsicmp( cls, buttonW ) && wcsicmp( cls, staticW )) return CLR_INVALID;
+    return fix;
+}
+
+INT WINAPI DrawTextExW( HDC hdc, LPWSTR str, INT i_count,
+                        LPRECT rect, UINT flags, LPDRAWTEXTPARAMS dtp )
+{
+    COLORREF fix = CLR_INVALID, old = CLR_INVALID;
+    INT ret;
+
+    if (str && !(flags & DT_CALCRECT) && (fix = neutron_readable_control_text( hdc )) != CLR_INVALID)
+        old = SetTextColor( hdc, fix );
+    ret = draw_text_ex_w( hdc, str, i_count, rect, flags, dtp );
+    if (old != CLR_INVALID) SetTextColor( hdc, old );
+    return ret;
+}
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *           DrawTextExA    (USER32.@)
  *
